---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const media = '/media/browser-handoff';
---
<section class="handoff-showcase wrap" id="recorded-browser-handoff" aria-labelledby="handoff-title" data-browser-handoff>
  <header class="handoff-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">A recorded browser handoff</p><h2 id="handoff-title">Same page.<br /><em>Different tab owners.</em></h2></div><p>Two tabs opened the same fictional brief. The extension selected Session A, the owner stored for the first tab. Sending it produced one request addressed to Session A.</p></header>
  <p class="handoff-scope">Actual ownership hook, Chrome extension and bridge in an isolated test. The session endpoint was a fixture; <strong>no agent read the page or replied.</strong></p>
  <div class="handoff-comparison">
    <div class="handoff-summary">
      <table><caption>Readable summary of the saved check</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Tab</th><th scope="col">Page address</th><th scope="col">Stored owner</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr data-handoff-tab-a><th scope="row">Tab A</th><td>Same address</td><td>Session A</td><td>Selected and sent</td></tr><tr data-handoff-tab-b><th scope="row">Tab B</th><td>Same address</td><td>Session B</td><td>Not sent</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <p class="handoff-result"><strong>One request · Session A</strong><span>Tab A’s browser identifiers retained.</span></p>
      <p class="handoff-explanation">The matching address did not choose the destination. The popup used the owner saved for the selected tab; the bridge routed that selected target.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="handoff-popup"><img src={`${media}/sent.png`} width="380" height="284" alt="Actual extension popup: Session A is marked opened this tab, and the result reads Sent to Session A." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Cropped desktop extension capture after Send. Endpoint and machine lines are masked; this is not a phone screenshot.</figcaption><a href={`${media}/sent.png`}>Inspect the popup at full size <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a></figure>
  </div>
  <details class="handoff-disclosure" data-handoff-film><summary>Watch the recorded handoff <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
    <figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster={`${media}/context.webp`} width="1360" height="900" aria-label="Recorded browser tab handoff" aria-describedby="handoff-film-caption"><source src={`${media}/execution.mp4`} type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src={`${media}/execution.vtt`} srclang="en" label="English action captions" default /><p><a href={`${media}/execution.mp4`}>Open the silent recording</a></p></video><figcaption id="handoff-film-caption">A continuous 8.40-second excerpt at original speed, including the brief confirmation. Endpoint and machine metadata are masked. The readable summary and popup still above preserve the result without playing the film.</figcaption></figure>
    <ol class="handoff-transcript"><li>Two tabs show the same fictional brief, grouped under Session A and Session B.</li><li>The real extension popup opens on Tab A and selects Session A, marked “opened this tab”.</li><li>Send produces one request to the fixture endpoint. The popup confirms “Sent to Session A”. No agent reads or answers the page.</li></ol>
  </div></details>
  <details class="handoff-disclosure handoff-method" data-handoff-method><summary>Source and test boundaries <Icon name="plus" /></summary><div>
    <p>Unchanged Metacodex <strong>v1.0.6</strong> ownership hook, extension popup and bridge, checked on 15 October 2026 in <strong>Chrome for Testing 156.0.8078.4</strong>. The popup was a genuine browser action popup, not an extension page opened as a tab.</p>
    <p>The original hook received synthetic tool events around real fixture-tab creation. The isolated browser had two synthetic session owners. Fleet discovery and terminal metadata were replaced with empty fixture results; infrastructure subprocesses were blocked. A local fake Unix app-server supplied the two sessions and recorded the request.</p>
    <p>The actual popup selected the stored owner and posted the chosen tab. The actual bridge validated the selected target, then sent one <code>turn/start</code> addressed to Session A. This is a request for a new turn, not an injected continuation of running inference. The bridge does not independently read browser ownership storage.</p>
    <p>No real Codex CLI, model, provider, page-reading tool or agent reply ran. Real session discovery, cross-machine delivery and downstream page-tool selection were not tested.</p>
    <p>The film retains original frames from 1.00 to 9.40 seconds, with no internal cuts or held ending. The popup still is an exact crop of the redacted film’s frame at 8.10 seconds, corresponding to 9.10 seconds in the original. Only endpoint and machine lines are masked; no screenshot pixels were regenerated.</p>
    <a href={`${media}/receipt.json`}>Read the concise execution receipt <Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></a>
  </div></details>
</section>
<script>
for (const showcase of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-browser-handoff]')) {
  const film = showcase.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('[data-handoff-film]');
  const video = film?.querySelector<HTMLVideoElement>('video');
  film?.addEventListener('toggle', () => { if (!film.open) video?.pause(); });
  window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => video?.pause());
}
</script>
<style>
.handoff-showcase{padding-block:24px 44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);scroll-margin-top:26px}.handoff-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:24px 56px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:22px}.handoff-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4.3vw,4rem);line-height:1.08}.handoff-intro h2 em{color:var(--forest)}.handoff-intro>p{font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);max-width:480px}.handoff-scope{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;padding:16px 20px;background:#edf0e4;border-left:3px solid var(--forest);margin-bottom:28px;max-width:1000px}.handoff-scope strong{font-weight:600}.handoff-comparison{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 380px;gap:32px 48px;align-items:start;margin-bottom:28px}.handoff-summary{min-width:0}.handoff-summary table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65}.handoff-summary caption{text-align:left;font-size:14px;font-weight:550;color:var(--muted);padding-bottom:14px}.handoff-summary :is(th,td){text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:14px 10px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.handoff-summary thead th{font-size:13px;font-weight:550;color:var(--muted)}.handoff-summary tbody th{font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap}.handoff-summary tbody tr:first-child{background:#edf0e4}.handoff-result{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:22px 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}.handoff-result strong,.handoff-result span{display:block}.handoff-result strong{font-weight:600;color:var(--forest-dark)}.handoff-result span{font-size:16px;margin-top:4px}.handoff-explanation{font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin-top:18px;max-width:600px}.handoff-popup{margin:0;min-width:0}.handoff-popup img{display:block;width:380px;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #b2baa6;border-radius:4px;background:white}.handoff-popup figcaption{font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--muted);margin-top:13px}.handoff-popup a,.handoff-method a{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:46px;font-size:14px;margin-top:4px}.handoff-popup :global(.ui-icon),.handoff-disclosure :global(.ui-icon){width:18px;height:18px;flex-shrink:0}.handoff-disclosure{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.handoff-disclosure:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.handoff-disclosure>summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;min-height:58px;padding:14px 4px;font-size:16px;font-weight:550;cursor:pointer}.handoff-disclosure[open]>summary :global(.ui-icon){transform:rotate(45deg)}.handoff-disclosure>div{padding:8px 0 24px}.handoff-disclosure figure{margin:0}.handoff-disclosure video{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:1360/900;background:#172221;border:1px solid #8d9b82;border-radius:4px}.handoff-disclosure video::cue{font-size:clamp(14px,1.6vw,24px);color:white;background:#172221}.handoff-disclosure figcaption,.handoff-method p,.handoff-transcript{font-size:15px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--muted);max-width:950px}.handoff-disclosure figcaption{margin-top:15px}.handoff-transcript{padding-left:22px;margin-top:18px}.handoff-transcript li+li{margin-top:8px}.handoff-method p{margin-bottom:15px}.handoff-method code{font-size:14px}.handoff-showcase :is(summary,a,video):focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--rust);outline-offset:4px}
@media(max-width:1000px){.handoff-comparison{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,380px);gap:28px}.handoff-summary :is(th,td){padding-inline:8px;font-size:14px}.handoff-summary thead th{font-size:12px}}
@media(max-width:760px){.handoff-showcase{padding-block:12px 34px}.handoff-intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}.handoff-intro h2{font-size:clamp(2.1rem,8vw,3.2rem)}.handoff-intro>p{font-size:16px;max-width:none}.handoff-scope{padding:14px 16px}.handoff-comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.handoff-summary :is(th,td){padding-inline:7px;font-size:14px}.handoff-summary thead th{font-size:12px}.handoff-popup{max-width:380px}.handoff-disclosure video:not(:fullscreen)::cue{font-size:14px}.handoff-result{font-size:18px}.handoff-disclosure>summary{font-size:15px}}
</style>
